WEBVTT

00:00:11.949 --> 00:00:12.717
Paying in Asia.

00:00:14.517 --> 00:00:16.778
In Asia, each market pays its own way,

00:00:17.119 --> 00:00:18.698
and most go through a local gateway of

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:19.441
their own.

00:00:19.594 --> 00:00:21.941
In one week, Asia was nearly a third

00:00:22.069 --> 00:00:23.861
of the card orders our payment service saw.

00:00:24.287 --> 00:00:25.098
Here is how they pay.

00:00:28.286 --> 00:00:29.438
Korea is the largest:

00:00:29.865 --> 00:00:31.059
more than half of those orders.

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:33.363
A card there can be charged at once,

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.881
or on an installment plan of two to

00:00:35.923 --> 00:00:36.623
seven months.

00:00:36.853 --> 00:00:38.645
And a customer can pay with no card

00:00:38.773 --> 00:00:39.350
at all:

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:41.589
a bank deposit, where the order waits for

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:42.331
the money.

00:00:45.328 --> 00:00:48.143
In Japan, every online card payment asks

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.424
for the bank's identity check.

00:00:50.021 --> 00:00:51.941
And customers can pay without a card there too:

00:00:52.368 --> 00:00:54.416
by bank transfer, or with a slip at

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:55.158
a convenience store.

00:00:58.331 --> 00:01:00.507
In Thailand, the checkout offers a second

00:01:00.635 --> 00:01:01.616
way to pay beside the card:

00:01:02.086 --> 00:01:03.579
PromptPay, a QR code.

00:01:04.091 --> 00:01:06.310
One sale in five there is paid that way.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:09.464
The shopper scans the code with a banking

00:01:09.592 --> 00:01:11.384
app, and has ten minutes to pay.

00:01:14.584 --> 00:01:15.907
In the Philippines and in India,

00:01:16.461 --> 00:01:18.125
the shopper leaves our checkout for the

00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:19.448
gateway's own payment page,

00:01:19.789 --> 00:01:20.856
and picks a way to pay there:

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:23.800
a card, a phone wallet, a bank transfer.

00:01:25.245 --> 00:01:26.738
Our payment service sees them leave.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:28.829
It does not always see them come back.

00:01:32.158 --> 00:01:34.376
And some of Asia never passes through our

00:01:34.419 --> 00:01:35.272
payment service at all:

00:01:35.827 --> 00:01:37.662
bank deposits, store slips,

00:01:38.174 --> 00:01:40.520
cash on delivery, and shops that charge

00:01:40.648 --> 00:01:41.374
the card themselves.

00:01:41.907 --> 00:01:43.998
In Hong Kong, Taiwan and Vietnam,

00:01:44.424 --> 00:01:45.790
in the two weeks we sampled,

00:01:46.131 --> 00:01:47.155
that was every payment.

00:01:49.565 --> 00:01:50.333
Paying in Asia:

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:52.552
each market has its own way to pay,

00:01:52.936 --> 00:01:55.239
often its own gateway, and not all of

00:01:55.282 --> 00:01:56.536
it passes through us.

